lects, flipping its vertical direction, and continues down‑left to (11,0).\n  - In pair 3 the beam goes down‑right to (7,7). The next cell, (8,8), is on the vertical 2‑wall. The beam reflects, flipping its horizontal direction, and continues down‑left to (14,0).\n\n**Which way does the beam reflect?** Suppose the beam is at (y,x) moving (dy,dx) and the next cell is a 2.\n- If (y+dy, x) is a 2, the wall is horizontal, so flip dy.\n- Otherwise, if (y, x+dx) is a 2, the wall is vertical, so flip dx.\n- Otherwise the beam has hit a wall end corner‑on, so flip both.\n\nAfter a reflection the beam may still be blocked, so the check repeats. This matters in test 1, where the beam zig‑zags between vertical walls.\n\n**Which end of the beam continues?** The end whose next diagonal cell is still inside the grid. The other end always points off the edge: (15,14) in pair 1, (0,0) in pair 3, (0,9) in test 2.\n\n## Applying it to the tests\n\n**Test 1.** The beam runs down‑right from (2,3).\n- It passes through the 3s at (3,4) and (7,8).\n- It meets 2‑walls at x=10 and x=7 and bounces between them several times.\n- It exits at about (15,12).\n\n**Test 2.** The beam runs down‑left from (2,7).\n- It reaches the 2‑wall at x=4, reflects, and heads down‑right.\n- It then passes through the 3‑wall at x=10.\n\n## Program\n\nThe program emits one checkpoint per straight segment (each ends at a bounce or at the grid edge) and then the final canvas.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid).copy()\n    H, W = g.shape\n    ones = sorted(zip(*np.where(g == 1)))\n    (y0, x0), (y1, x1) = ones[0], ones[-1]\n    sdy = 1 if y1 > y0 else (-1 if y1 < y0 else 0)\n    sdx = 1 if x1 > x0 else (-1 if x1 < x0 else 0)\n    if len(ones) == 1:\n        sdy, sdx = 1, 1\n    def inb(y, x):\n        return 0 <= y < H and 0 <= x < W\n    # choose the end whose continuation stays in the grid\n    if inb(y1 + sdy, x1 + sdx):\n        y, x, dy, dx = y1, x1, sdy, sdx\n    else:\n        y, x, dy, dx = y0, x0, -sdy, -sdx\n    steps = 0\n    while steps < 2000:\n        steps += 1\n        ny, nx = y + dy, x + dx\n        if not inb(ny, nx):\n            break\n        if g[ny, nx] == 2:\n            # reflect off the mirror wall\n            if inb(y + dy, x) and g[y + dy, x] == 2:\n                dy = -dy\n            elif inb(y, x + dx) and g[y, x + dx] == 2:\n                dx = -dx\n            else:\n                dy, dx = -dy, -dx\n            emit(g, f\"Beam hits a colour-2 mirror at ({ny},{nx}); it reflects to direction ({dy},{dx}).\")\n            continue\n        g[ny, nx] = 1  # empty cell or transparent colour-3 wall\n        y, x = ny, nx\n    emit(g, \"Beam has travelled diagonally until leaving the grid, passing through 3s and bouncing off 2s.\")\n    return g\n","candidate_tactics":{"rigid":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- **Colour 2 is a mirror.**"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Which way does the beam reflect?** Suppose the beam is at (y,x) moving (dy,dx) and the next cell is a 2."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"After a reflection the beam may still be blocked, so the check repeats."}],"repeat":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"This matters in test 1, where the beam zig‑zags between vertical walls."}],"rays":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- a short diagonal run of **1** cells (a \"beam\" that has already started),"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"In every output the beam keeps going diagonally from its open end until it leaves the grid."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- **Colour 3 is transparent.** In pair 2 the beam travels down‑left from (5,11) and reaches (8,8), which is part of the 3‑wall."}],"dynamics":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- It meets 2‑walls at x=10 and x=7 and bounces between them several times."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The program emits one checkpoint per straight segment (each ends at a bounce or at the grid edge) and then the final canvas."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Beam has travelled diagonally until leaving the grid, passing through 3s and bouncing off 2s."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"4ba64984aeeaea5ce9e92445fa705d4286a40fac43db364ee235fe04976e1113","task_sha256":"a94c14e91a4d50eec0f3a782b0d117ee07f9a652ccb8fbca8c3fa45a87a3afd8","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
